course: dictionary
lesson: 9245
title: Sorghum, a crop for hot, dry places
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sometimes you will meet a word you have never seen, like sorghum. The words around it are its context, and they often give you clues. In «Farming began separately in several places: wheat in the Middle East, rice in China, maize in Mexico, potatoes in the Andes, bananas and taro in New Guinea, sorghum in Africa.», the list tells you that sorghum is something people farm.
explain: Look at the other items in the list: wheat, rice, maize and potatoes are all crops that people grow for food. So sorghum must be a crop too. Ask yourself: what kind of word fits here? Sorghum is a thing, a noun, because it is placed in a list of things that were farmed.
explain: Now test your idea by putting it back into the sentence. "Farming began in Africa for a crop called sorghum" still makes sense, so your meaning works. If you are still not sure, a dictionary will tell you that sorghum is a tall cereal grass grown for its grain, its sweet juice and animal feed.
fact: Sorghum is a tall cereal grass.
fact: Sorghum grows well in warm, dry countries, especially in Africa and Asia, where wheat and rice struggle.
fact: People use sorghum grain for food, its sweet juice for sweetener, and the plant as animal feed.
fact: Sorghum syrup is a sweetener, and sorghum flour is gluten-free.
exercise: The text says «sorghum in Africa». What does this tell you about sorghum? | It is a kind of sea fish | *It is a crop people farm, like wheat and rice | It is an animal that lives in the desert | It is a city in Africa
exercise: Where does sorghum grow best, according to the dictionary? | Cold, wet mountains | *Warm, dry countries | Under the sea | Inside a freezing city
exercise: Find and copy one other crop named in the sentence, besides sorghum. | Middle | places | *rice | separately
test: Which of these is a tall cereal grass grown for its grain, juice and feed? | *Sorghum | Andes | Maize | Taro
test: In the USA, what is sorghum syrup used for? | Glue for paper | Fuel for cars | *A sweetener | Paint for walls
exam: Using the sentence and what you know, what is the best meaning of sorghum? | A sea animal | *A grain crop grown in hot, dry places | A coloured paint | A kind of boat
